;; plan-ancestry.edn -- the operative plan artifacts of the WM build, and the
;; ancestry each one pins. Schema from N-process-trap-recording-conventions.md:267
;; (§3, "Ancestry and surfacing fields (F5)"); mechanism from
;; DRIFT-2026-09-05-account.md:125 (§4-§5), where the R5 spine was displaced with
;; no actor-authored decision and no field in which such a decision could have
;; been recorded.
;;
;; Checked by: bb ancestry_check.bb  (called from worklist_check.bb, so the loop
;; runs it before a seat takes a row).
;;
;; Fields, per §3:
;;   :artifact                 repo-relative path of the plan (must exist)
;;   :ancestor/commissioning   file or file:line the plan descends from (must resolve)
;;   :clauses/declared         clause ids THIS plan declares, each with a pointer
;;   :clauses/inherited        clause ids carried forward from the ancestor
;;   :clauses/dropped          {:clause :by :at :decision/not-done} -- all four required
;;   :deps/derived             [[producer consumer] ...] over the ids in :order
;;                             (clause ids, or the nouns a spine plan schedules)
;;   :order                    the schedule the plan declares, if it declares one
;;   :notify/required?         whether this record must be surfaced (T6)
;;   :notify/discharged-at     the surfacing event id -- not a timestamp alone
;;
;; JURISDICTION. :grandfathered true means the plan predates the F5 gate: what it
;; DECLARES is still checked in full (pointers resolve; a dropped clause carries
;; its four fields; an inherited clause is one the ancestor actually declares; no
;; consumer is ordered before its producer), but a clause of its ancestor that is
;; neither inherited nor dropped is REPORTED as unaccounted rather than refused.
;; A plan minted after the gate refuses on the same finding. Same rule as the
;; worklist rows: grandfathering excuses an absence, never a falsehood.
{:schema :wm/plan-ancestry-v1
 :as-of "2026-09-05"
 :repo "futon2"
